# SUPPLEMENT to gen_fu_l37_tag_eor_corrigendum.log (committed 726682a, md5 467980032e371c2e332a3e1c1e5cc242).
# That corrigendum is RETAINED and stays closed. This carries the two CR-35 rows that arrived after it was
# committed: L-2, the mutation's applied diff, and M-1, the excused-miss red.
# WHY A SUPPLEMENT: landing 39 committed at 20:13:33Z and I edited the corrigendum at 20:19Z on rows that arrived
# after the hand-off, before the confirmation reached me. Its committed bytes were restored from the commit and
# verified, and the added text lives here. Same lesson as the landing-36 supplement records: after a hand-off a
# listed file changes only after a withdrawal is acknowledged.
#
# ================ CR-35-L-2: the mutation's applied diff is retained ================
# The landing-37 log cites gen_tb_top.sv 736a8d8099339024 before MUT-ALERTSUP and 85b50e1343c65af1 after, and the
# diff was not in the tree, so neither figure could be reproduced. It is retained as
# gen_fu_l39_MUTALERTSUP_mutant.diff with its own manifest row, in the gen_fu_l13 convention. Both digests below are
# measured from the files, and the diff is shown to apply to a detached archive of the commit.
#
# ================ CR-35-M-1: the excused-miss red is NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE, and now by MEASUREMENT ================
# The row asks for a genuine missing alert that landing 37's predicate would excuse and landing 39's fails: an
# injection with no retirement at or after it whose window nonetheless closes before the last observed cycle. That
# needs the TAIL, last observed cycle minus last retirement, to EXCEED GEN_ICACHE_ECC_WINDOW, which is 2.
# THE TAIL IS EXACTLY 2, measured rather than inferred. A scratch probe printing misc.cycle at the misc monitor's
# report phase, one $display and nothing else, reports the last observed cycle as 21480, against a last retirement
# of 21478 read from the same run's export. The earlier corrigendum could only bound it at "at most 2" from the
# allowance's own verdict; this measures it.
# SO THE WINDOW IS EMPTY BY EXACTLY ONE CYCLE: the case needs an injection cycle c with c > 21478 and c + 2 <= 21480,
# which is c <= 21478. Contradiction. One more observed cycle in the tail and the case would exist.
# AND IT IS NOT A PROPERTY OF ONE SEED: six seeds show the interrupt checker's checked-cycle count sitting exactly
# one below the last retirement in every run, so the observing window closes at the last retirement in all of them.
# WHY THE TAIL WAS NOT LENGTHENED TO MANUFACTURE THE CASE: extending the settle until the window fits would be
# building the fixture to fit the rule, the failure mode this whole sequence has been about. The negative is reported
# with its figures for the Critic to judge.

